# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets & credentials
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Blanket .txt rule retained from the original file. It is the reason
# node-token.txt was never committed, so it stays as defence-in-depth.
# Cost is only that prose .txt files must be named .md instead.
*.txt

# Explicit guards (these are the ones that matter; *.txt is a backstop)
node-token.txt
k3s_node_token.txt
kubeconfig
kubeconfig.*
*.kubeconfig
.kube/
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
!*.pub

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Benchmark output
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-run directories total ~3.3 GB and are regenerated by harness/.
# The bulk (raw VM exports) stays out of git; the results/ summaries are kept,
# because they are the evidence a claim in the paper rests on and they are a
# few kB each. A summary in git with no raw data is still auditable for the
# numbers it reports, and the run_id inside it identifies the raw directory.
# Deliberately EXCLUDED from this rule (kept in git as paper-1 baseline data):
#   benchmarks/1-node/                     — per-device + distribution CSVs
#   benchmarks/generate_benchmark_csv.py   — regenerates the above
benchmarks/*
!benchmarks/1-node/
!benchmarks/generate_benchmark_csv.py
# NOTE: results/ summaries are ignored along with the raw exports. The
# corrected runs are committed explicitly with `git add -f` rather than by a
# blanket negation, because a negation would also sweep in the ~600 historical
# summaries -- and those were produced by the tooling that D4, D9, D11 and D15
# show to be wrong. Committing them unannotated would imply they are citable.
# The two corrected runs are benchmarks/20260930_115549 (QoS 0) and
# benchmarks/20260930_120326 (QoS 1); see docs/findings-p0.md.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build artifacts
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# publisher/consumer are compiled by `make`; consumer.go / publisher.c are the
# sources of truth and remain tracked.
publisher
consumer
*.gz
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.oelf

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tooling caches
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Manuscript sources
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The paper is built from LaTeX and has its own repository. Compiled PDFs are
# not part of the code artifact.
*.pdf

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local scratch
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.swp
.DS_Store
reports/
